@cloudflare is doing enormous disservice to customers by blocking websites by default from AI. If you have personal or business websites, they become invisible to AI by default! 

This can literally kill your business or career.  I'm fairly technical and even I just found out several of my domains were blocked to AI crawlers totally unintentionally after I moved things over to cloudflare.

They apparently went totally overboard in responding shenanigans from "creator" community.

@eastdakota @CloudflareDev - seriously, fix this!!

In the Code Arena: WebDev, @OpenAI's  GPT-6 Astra (Max) is ranked #1 (1800 pts), and Claude Fable 5.1 (Max) is ranked #2 (1758 pts). Here is a look at win rates for these models.

Win rate measures how often people prefer one model’s response in Arena’s anonymous head-to-head battles. Against the other models shown, Astra clearly wins most battles, including 72.5% against GPT-5.6 Sol (xHigh).

@AnthropicAI's Claude Fable 5.1 is the exception. Fable 5.1 wins 43.5% of battles, Astra wins 29.0%, and 27.4% of battles between them end in ties. Despite Astra's #1 ranking, Fable 5.1 is the preferred model when their outputs are compared head-to-head by Arena's users.
